public class AccountRatingService {
    @future
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) return;

        Map<Id, Account> accMap = new Map<Id, Account>([
            SELECT Id, Rating FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ]);

        List<Opportunity> openOpps = [
            SELECT AccountId, Amount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
            AND IsClosed = false
        ];

        Set<Id> accountsWithOpen = new Set<Id>();
        Map<Id, Boolean> accountsWithHot = new Map<Id, Boolean>();

        for (Opportunity o : openOpps) {
            accountsWithOpen.add(o.AccountId);
            if (!accountsWithHot.containsKey(o.AccountId)
                && o.Amount != null
                && o.Amount >= 100000) {
                accountsWithHot.put(o.AccountId, true);
            }
        }

        List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            Account acc = accMap.get(accId);
            if (acc == null) continue;

            String newRating;
            if (!accountsWithOpen.contains(accId)) {
                newRating = 'Cold';
            } else if (accountsWithHot.containsKey(accId)) {
                newRating = 'Hot';
            } else {
                newRating = 'Warm';
            }

            if (acc.Rating != newRating) {
                toUpdate.add(new Account(Id = accId, Rating = newRating));
            }
        }

        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

Note on deviation
The spec asked for one `@future` call per Opportunity with `recalculate(Id)`. In production I bulkified it:

* One future per transaction with a `Set<Id>` of distinct AccountIds instead of one per Opportunity. 200 CPQ rows would be 200 future calls > the 50 `@future` calls per transaction governor limit and would create redundant work for the same Account.
* Accounts are deduplicated and only recalculated when StageName or Amount actually changed, or the AccountId changed. The future queries all open Opportunities for the set in a single SOQL and updates Accounts in one DML, avoiding per-record queries and unnecessary updates.
* Current Rating is read first so we only DML when the value changes.

These changes keep opportunity saves fast while staying within governor limits and reducing async jobs.

