        Set<Id> changedAccountIds = new Set<Id>();
        Map<Id, String> newCountryById = new Map<Id, String>();
        Map<Id, String> oldCountryById = new Map<Id, String>();

        for (Account acc : newAccounts) {
            Account oldAcc = oldMap.get(acc.Id);
            if (oldAcc == null) continue;
            if (acc.BillingCountry != oldAcc.BillingCountry) {
                changedAccountIds.add(acc.Id);
                newCountryById.put(acc.Id, acc.BillingCountry);
                oldCountryById.put(acc.Id, oldAcc.BillingCountry);
            }
        }

        if (changedAccountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        List<Contact> contactsToUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Contact con : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :changedAccountIds
        ]) {
            String oldCountry = oldCountryById.get(con.AccountId);
            String newCountry = newCountryById.get(con.AccountId);
            String mailingCountry = con.MailingCountry;

            Boolean isBlank = String.isBlank(mailingCountry);
            Boolean isSameAsOld = mailingCountry == oldCountry;

            if (isBlank || isSameAsOld) {
                if (newCountry != mailingCountry) {
                    con.MailingCountry = newCountry;
                    contactsToUpdate.add(con);
                }
            }
        }

        if (!contactsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update contactsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

Why the approach was changed:
Querying `[SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry FROM Contact]` for the whole org would load all 2.3M contacts. That exceeds the 50,000-row SOQL limit, heap limits and CPU time, and is unnecessary. The handler now only queries contacts for the Account Ids whose BillingCountry actually changed in this transaction. This is bulk-safe, respects governor limits, and still updates only contacts whose MailingCountry is blank or equals the account’s previous BillingCountry, leaving abroad contacts untouched.

